      "id": "020HeelFit",
      "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nEdit target: the attached full-body Cartoon Johnny sprite, 1024x1536 RGBA. The walking pose and character design have been approved. Make one very small silhouette clearance correction only.\nOn the planted RIGHT foot at the bottom of the picture, the SCREEN-RIGHT outer heel contour near x720-728, y1380-1440 sticks slightly too far sideways. Bring this rightmost heel outline inward toward screen-left by about 14 source pixels, gently blending into the existing ankle and sole. Keep the heel rounded and anatomically natural. This is roughly one outline-width adjustment to that small heel bulge, not moving the whole foot or shortening the leg. Leave the toes at the screen-left end of this planted foot unchanged, and keep its flat ground contact and sole height unchanged.\nPreserve the other raised LEFT foot exactly, including its smooth side contour, single distal toe group, downward orientation and strong knee bend. No extra side toes. Keep the leg order, shorts, arms, torso, hair, beard, face and cap unchanged. Preserve the exact canvas dimensions, cap position, drawing scale and character placement. No whole-body recentering or shrinking, no pose redesign.\nReturn one complete sprite on genuine transparent alpha, with no added background, halo, shadow, text or marks.",
